# SOLID & Clean Code (Mandatory)

## SOLID

- **S — Single Responsibility**: One class/function = one reason to change.
- **O — Open/Closed**: Extend via new classes (Service, Action, Policy), not by editing working code.
- **L — Liskov Substitution**: Implementations must honor interface contracts (e.g. `FamilyRepositoryInterface`).
- **I — Interface Segregation**: Small focused interfaces; avoid fat service classes.
- **D — Dependency Inversion**: Controllers depend on abstractions; bind in `AppServiceProvider`.

## Clean code rules

- Meaningful names in English for code; Arabic for user-facing strings only.
- Functions ≤ 20 lines; classes ≤ 200 lines — split when larger.
- No magic numbers/strings — use constants, enums, or config.
- No commented-out code; no dead imports.
- DRY: extract repeated logic to Service, Concern, Hook, or Lib.
- Fail fast: validate early, throw domain exceptions with clear messages.
- Prefer explicit over clever; readability over brevity.

## Examples

```php
// ❌ BAD — logic in controller
public function store(Request $request) {
    Family::create($request->all());
}

// ✅ GOOD — delegate to action/service
public function store(StoreFamilyRequest $request, StoreFamilyAction $action) {
    $action->execute($request->validated());
    return redirect()->route('families.index');
}
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — fetch inside leaf component
function FamilyRow() { const [data, setData] = useState(); useEffect(() => fetch...); }

// ✅ GOOD — data from page via props or Inertia shared props
function FamilyRow({ family }: { family: Family }) { ... }
```
